  <%!-- ===== FAQ ===== --%>
  <section class="border-b border-(--crit-border)">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-24 px-10 max-sm:px-4 max-sm:py-12">
      <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-(--crit-brand) mb-3 text-center">
        Common questions
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-12 text-center max-sm:text-2xl">
        The bits people ask before they buy.
      </h2>
      <div class="bg-(--crit-bg-card) border border-(--crit-border) rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <details open class="border-b border-(--crit-border) group">
          <summary class="list-none cursor-pointer py-5 px-6 flex items-center gap-3 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-(--crit-fg-muted) shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
            >
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-(--crit-fg-primary)">
              Can I self-host Crit Organizations?
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="pb-[22px] px-6 pl-12 text-sm text-(--crit-fg-secondary) leading-relaxed">
            Yes &mdash; organizations are included in every self-hosted deployment. Follow the <a href={~p"/self-hosting"} class="text-(--crit-brand) no-underline hover:underline">self-hosting guide</a> to get started.
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="border-b border-(--crit-border) group">
          <summary class="list-none cursor-pointer py-5 px-6 flex items-center gap-3 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-(--crit-fg-muted) shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
            >
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-(--crit-fg-primary)">
              Do I need an account for the CLI to work?
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="pb-[22px] px-6 pl-12 text-sm text-(--crit-fg-secondary) leading-relaxed">
            No. The CLI is fully local. Sharing &mdash; solo or via an org &mdash; is the only thing that touches a server. Skip sharing and Crit never phones home.
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="border-b border-(--crit-border) group">
          <summary class="list-none cursor-pointer py-5 px-6 flex items-center gap-3 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-(--crit-fg-muted) shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
            >
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-(--crit-fg-primary)">
              What happens when someone leaves the org?
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="pb-[22px] px-6 pl-12 text-sm text-(--crit-fg-secondary) leading-relaxed">
            An admin removes their membership. Reviews they shared into the org stay with the org. Their personal reviews stay with them.
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="group">
          <summary class="list-none cursor-pointer py-5 px-6 flex items-center gap-3 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-(--crit-fg-muted) shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
            >
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-(--crit-fg-primary)">
              Is my code ever sent to a server?
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="pb-[22px] px-6 pl-12 text-sm text-(--crit-fg-secondary) leading-relaxed">
            Only the file contents you explicitly include in a shared review. Everything else &mdash; drafts, comments-in-progress, agent context &mdash; stays local.
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ===== CTA ===== --%>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto py-28 px-10 max-sm:px-4 max-sm:py-12 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight leading-tight text-balance max-sm:text-3xl">
        Get the team in the agent loop<span class="text-(--crit-brand)">.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-(--crit-fg-secondary) leading-relaxed mt-6 mb-10 max-w-xl mx-auto max-sm:text-base">
        Free during the beta. Set up takes under a minute &mdash; create an org, invite teammates, share your first review.
      </p>
      <div class="flex gap-2.5 justify-center flex-wrap max-sm:flex-col max-sm:items-stretch">
        <a
          href={~p"/orgs/new"}
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-7 py-3 bg-(--crit-brand-cta) text-(--crit-fg-on-brand) rounded-lg text-sm font-bold no-underline hover:bg-(--crit-brand-cta-hover) transition-all"
        >
          Create an organization <.icon name="hero-arrow-right-mini" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/tomasz-tomczyk/crit"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-7 py-3 border border-(--crit-border) text-(--crit-fg-secondary) rounded-lg text-sm font-semibold no-underline hover:border-(--crit-fg-muted) hover:text-(--crit-fg-primary) transition-all"
        >
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            class="w-[13px] h-[13px]"
            fill="currentColor"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path d="M12 .5C5.65.5.5 5.65.5 12c0 5.08 3.29 9.39 7.86 10.92.58.1.79-.25.79-.56v-2c-3.2.7-3.87-1.36-3.87-1.36-.52-1.34-1.28-1.7-1.28-1.7-1.05-.71.08-.7.08-.7 1.16.08 1.78 1.2 1.78 1.2 1.03 1.77 2.7 1.26 3.36.96.1-.75.4-1.26.73-1.55-2.55-.29-5.24-1.28-5.24-5.7 0-1.26.45-2.29 1.18-3.1-.12-.29-.51-1.47.11-3.06 0 0 .97-.31 3.18 1.18a11 11 0 0 1 5.78 0c2.21-1.49 3.18-1.18 3.18-1.18.62 1.59.23 2.77.11 3.06.74.81 1.18 1.84 1.18 3.1 0 4.44-2.7 5.41-5.26 5.69.41.36.78 1.06.78 2.14v3.17c0 .31.21.67.8.55C20.21 21.38 23.5 17.07 23.5 12 23.5 5.65 18.35.5 12 .5z" />
          </svg>
          Star on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
